{
  "format": "gt-toolz-voice-packages",
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Optional voice packages. The app offers them at first start (and in settings): packages for the app language are preselected, the user deselects what they do not want. Downloads start only after the user confirms. Windows voices need no package.",
    "Only voices whose license clearly allows use in GT Toolz (free, closed source, donations without perks). Decisions 2026-10-18, see docs/dev/security.md.",
    "Rejected Piper voices: en_US-lessac (research only) and everything finetuned from it (ryan, kerstin, thorsten, amy).",
    "Both engines contain espeak-ng (GPL-3.0-or-later). Users download them from the original source; GT Toolz only runs them as separate programs.",
    "Engines come per platform (\"platform\": \"<os>-<arch>\" as Node reports it, e.g. \"win32-x64\", \"linux-x64\"); voice models are the same everywhere. A package without a file for the running platform is not offered.",
    "Added 2026-10-24 from ReadMyChat (the user: only voices free for open-source use, licenses checked again at the sources): standard licenses only (MIT, BSD, Apache, CC0 or public domain, CC BY with attribution). English Piper voices by Bryce Beattie, trained from scratch on public-domain recordings (LibriVox, LJ Speech; John finetuned from Kristin), MIT in rhasspy/piper-voices and \"public domain\" on his page; CSS10 German (BSD-3-Clause, dataset CC0), runs in sherpa-onnx without espeak.",
    "Removed 2026-10-24 (supply-chain and licence audit, the user's choice): Kokoro-82M. Its weights are Apache-2.0, but its training data includes synthetic audio generated by closed TTS models of unknown origin, and unclear counts as no. English now preselects Piper Kristin (coach) and Norman (crew); sherpa-onnx remains for CSS10 German.",
    "2026-10-24: macOS. Piper's own macOS build does not start (rhasspy/piper#404), so the Mac gets sherpa-onnx 1.13.8 (osx-arm64 and osx-x64 shared builds) and the Piper voices as sherpa-onnx packages them (tts-models: the same voice, with tokens.txt and espeak-ng-data). Not packaged there: de_DE-mls-medium (Jan). Plus the macOS system voices (no download). SHA-256 and sizes computed from the downloads; they match GitHub's asset digests."
  ],
